  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This can lead to the operating system running out of file handles.  Reported by Janna Wemekamp on the fcrepo-user list.  More information and reproduce: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://fedora-commons.1317035.n2.nabble.com/fcrepo-user-FedoraCommons-3-4-with-Akubra-Low-Level-Storage-Java-crash-in-REST-API-s-getNextPID-td5480759.html"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://fedora-commons.1317035.n2.nabble.com/fcrepo-user-FedoraCommons-3-4-with-Akubra-Low-Level-Storage-Java-crash-in-REST-API-s-getNextPID-td5480759.html",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This problem does not occur when the old AuthN (non-FeSL) is used, so if using fedora-users.xml with Fedora 3.4, it is recommended to answer \"false\" to \"Enable FeSL AuthN?\" at install time.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
