  "description": "<p>This can lead to the operating system running out of file handles.  Reported by Janna Wemekamp on the fcrepo-user list.  More information and reproduce: <a href=\"http://fedora-commons.1317035.n2.nabble.com/fcrepo-user-FedoraCommons-3-4-with-Akubra-Low-Level-Storage-Java-crash-in-REST-API-s-getNextPID-td5480759.html\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fedora-commons.1317035.n2.nabble.com/fcrepo-user-FedoraCommons-3-4-with-Akubra-Low-Level-Storage-Java-crash-in-REST-API-s-getNextPID-td5480759.html</a></p>\n\n<p>This problem does not occur when the old AuthN (non-FeSL) is used, so if using fedora-users.xml with Fedora 3.4, it is recommended to answer \"false\" to \"Enable FeSL AuthN?\" at install time.</p>",
